    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d30d45_797a6329",
        "filename": "chip/lm4/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-08T14:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. I wasn\u0027t sure what to do here. The problem is if somebody changes code in the future that enables or disables the clock to one of the peripherals after startup, then it would cause a bug here because that change wouldn\u0027t get carried over. So, I put this in to see what people thought about it.",
      "parentUuid": "61c0fd68_a0931ea7",
      "revId": "83fc1988fba0e1c41be7a2dda5ff155946f38676",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d30d45_195b6ffe",
        "filename": "chip/lm4/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-08T01:39:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why ?",
      "revId": "83fc1988fba0e1c41be7a2dda5ff155946f38676",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d30d45_5977a73d",
        "filename": "chip/lm4/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-08T14:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GPIO block K has to get a clock in order to generate an interrupt when a keyboard button is pressed. I found this out the hard way. Without this, some key presses are ignored because it happens to be in deep sleep when button is pressed.",
      "parentUuid": "e1d30d45_195b6ffe",
      "revId": "83fc1988fba0e1c41be7a2dda5ff155946f38676",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
