    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d30d45_9cdbed38",
        "filename": "chip/lm4/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 238,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-08T14:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, looking at this more closely, the place interrupts need to be disabled is in the calling function around the call to this function and the enabling of the interrupt. The problem is if we get an interrupt after setting the match register and before enabling the RTC interrupt, then by the time we enable the RTC interrupt, we could have already passed the match time and then we will not see the RTC interrupt for a very long time (until it rolls over I think).",
      "parentUuid": "e1d30d45_39c2ab43",
      "revId": "83fc1988fba0e1c41be7a2dda5ff155946f38676",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
